{"title":"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are fixed such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> lies on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, closer to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c342fbb42e9510a8b01974ba4437a455b30a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AT=m$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/c/0dc39d8a071837c01c04ac9e690ed9a6af503b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BT=n$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers. Construct circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with a variable radius that is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point such that circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the incircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90f6a92b773f52f528b404bd0d2712a65f105073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> as the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be728aed505b28aaff3aa0b23debd2ec6172a72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" /> denote the maximum value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74104283f6bf1d36bd56d7b7ce76359e0c6b6209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^{2}\\angle AMP$\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> for fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb2b326840add3c30cfa0bba450b44959d46f64e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aad4c9b0d9d361aa3165d1d815f70410f512f3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m,49)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> is an integer, find the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Please see below an attempted solution to understand why this problem doesn't have a solution:\n</p><p>Lemma: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f8345784b1eae8e20a5bac5031620e9024a07e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{B}-\\cot{A}=2\\cot{\\angle{AMP}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"231\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Proof of lemma: \n</p><p>Construct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/590bf37717ce66f41aa794c0cbaac567fd7f32e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PH\\perp{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>Case (i) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/5/ad5648c2a2a7813a582917039b6a328c55de44b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&lt;90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d55fbc1eb76ce6d6c4766769558d775c1d60cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{B}-\\cot{A}=\\dfrac{BH}{PH}-\\dfrac{AH}{PH}=\\dfrac{BM+MH}{PH}-\\dfrac{AM-MH}{PH}=\\dfrac{BM+MH-AM+MH}{PH}=\\dfrac{2MH}{PH}=\\cot{\\angle{AMP}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"883\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Case (ii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/35952796bdc5181ab69ebf7344f4c9070365fc78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&gt;90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/2453e6922c3abb9b47e8e5f31c4ee2d2675b1215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{B}-\\cot{A}=\\dfrac{BH}{PH}+\\dfrac{AH}{PH}=\\dfrac{BM+MH}{PH}+\\dfrac{MH-AM}{PH}=\\dfrac{BM+MH-AM+MH}{PH}=\\dfrac{2MH}{PH}=\\cot{\\angle{AMP}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"883\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Case (iii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07adab0487fd9b8c5bb970e717d025523f72123.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=90^\\circ$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec644bd7ee8a5f8eb7b96e13e431e935ff056da3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot{B}-\\cot{A}=\\dfrac{BA}{PA}-0=\\dfrac{2MA}{PA}=\\cot{\\angle{AMP}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"377\" height=\"39\" />,  proof done.\n</p><p><br />\nNow we try to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be728aed505b28aaff3aa0b23debd2ec6172a72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"62\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Let O be the centre of the incircle,  and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the inradius.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19b97c747591909c5fbe788a1274afa6d184d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\angle{OAB}} = \\dfrac{OT}{AT} = \\dfrac{r}{m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"187\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/e/33e836ea97ae46c8cc0cef1349f9c0a3e2964fb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\angle{PAB}} = \\tan{(2\\angle{OAB})} =  \\dfrac{2\\tan{\\angle{OAB}}}{1-\\tan^2{\\angle{OAB}}} = \\dfrac{2r/m}{1-(r/m)^2} = \\dfrac{2mr}{m^2-r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"576\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Similarly,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b052352070de6e63571d177aaaeed6ed8dcb5e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{\\angle{PBA}} = \\dfrac{2nr}{n^2-r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"171\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92e5aa062df948a78a392a512080ae0d6074f73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2{\\angle{AMP}} = \\dfrac{1}{\\cot^2{\\angle{AMP}}} = \\dfrac{1}{\\dfrac{(\\cot{\\angle{PBA}}-\\cot{\\angle{PAB}})^2}{2^2}} = \\dfrac{4}{(\\cot{\\angle{PBA}}-\\cot{\\angle{PAB}})^2} = \\dfrac{4}{\\Big(\\dfrac{1}{\\tan{\\angle{PBA}}}-\\dfrac{1}{\\tan{\\angle{PAB}}}\\Big)^2} = \\dfrac{4}{\\Big(\\dfrac{n^2-r^2}{2nr}-\\dfrac{m^2-r^2}{2mr}\\Big)^2} = \\dfrac{16m^2n^2r^2}{[(n^2-r^2)m-(m^2-r^2)n]^2} = \\dfrac{16m^2n^2r^2}{[(n-m)(r^2+mn)]^2} \\le \\dfrac{16m^2n^2r^2}{[(n-m)(2r\\sqrt{mn})]^2} = \\dfrac{4mn}{n-m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -38px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1539f2ce7c3d2ed18d94e6c4862eb6c7f738c45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m,49)=\\dfrac{196m}{49-m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"154\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> are 48, 47, 42, 35, and the answer is 48+47+42+35=172.\n</p><p>What's the problem with this solution?\n</p><p>When AM-GM was used, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f10b4adbc8c5dadc5741a4af0eef7f4948babd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\sqrt{mn}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" /> is when \"=\" is achieved. However, in this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e7c591f0e6173e2c65c2d1400f8db2c9f3a9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PA\\parallel{PB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, so contradiction. \n</p><p>If the phrase \"maximum value\" in the original problem is changed to \"least upper bound of\", then the problem should have the solution above. \n</p><p>~Di Xu\n</p>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 13\"> Previous Problem</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 15\"> Next Problem</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_1_2006-2007\" title=\"Mock AIME 1 2006-2007\">Mock AIME 1 2006-2007</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018035528\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.019 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 187/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8659/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3516:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018035528 and revision id 205259. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}